{title: To the Ends of the Earth}
{subtitle: Acts 1:8}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Gathered around him in the quiet hall
They asked about the time of the [Bb]kingdom's call
[Dm]He spoke of seasons only [C]the Father knows
[Bb]Times set apart by his [Dm]own authority
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You will re[Bb]ceive power [F]when the Spirit [C]comes
Witnesses [Dm]in Jerusalem, [Bb]Judea, Samaria
[F]Carrying the light to [C]the ends of the [Dm]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
As they watched in wonder he was [C]lifted high
[Dm]A cloud took him from their [Bb]sight and memory
[Dm]Two men in white robes stood [C]beside them then
[Bb]Speaking of the promise [Dm]of his return
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You will re[Bb]ceive power [F]when the Spirit [C]comes
Witnesses [Dm]in Jerusalem, [Bb]Judea, Samaria
[F]Carrying the light to the [C]ends of the [Dm]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Why do you stand here [Dm]looking into the sky
[Bb]He who has gone in[Dm]to heaven will [Bb]return
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]Power from the Ho[Bb]ly [F]Spirit on [C]you
To the [Dm]ends of the [Bb][F]earth
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
